{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_11","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run/draft && sed -n '1,40p' update-02.json\"","aggregated_output":"{\n  \"rationale\": \"The registered experiment for @q-snapshot-boundary was executed by the controller and produced a retained receipt (CheckRun 72367650c8d0470d8197a7d2c0f97ce1, exit 0, outcome tests_passed). This update interprets that receipt, promotes the observed instance to a Fact, and keeps the leader-side loop as an open necessary gap rather than assuming it.\",\n  \"sources\": [\n    { \"id\": \"src-installsnap2\", \"file\": \"raft.go\", \"start_line\": 1814, \"end_line\": 1953, \"kind\": \"code_observation\" },\n    { \"id\": \"src-lastindex2\", \"file\": \"state.go\", \"start_line\": 157, \"end_line\": 174, \"kind\": \"code_observation\" },\n    { \"id\": \"src-appendentries2\", \"file\": \"raft.go\", \"start_line\": 1475, \"end_line\": 1502, \"kind\": \"code_observation\" }\n  ],\n  \"knowledge\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"c4f67dac947d44fe86d65b317d5d5b4-question-0\",\n      \"ref\": \"@q-snapshot-boundary\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"src-installsnap2\", \"src-lastindex2\", \"src-appendentries2\"],\n      \"hypothesis\": \"Reconfirmed against the retained receipt: the follower keeps the log-derived term for the snapshot index and therefore rejects the leader's boundary AppendEntries; the leader-facing retry cycle remains source-sourced pending its own execution.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"ref\": \"@b-executed-boundary-witness\",\n      \"kind\": \"fact\",\n      \"statement\": \"In the executed harness, after a successful InstallSnapshot with LastLogIndex=2/LastLogTerm=3, the defect-case node (which had earlier stored a term-2 command at index 2) reported last_log_index=2, last_log_term=2, last_snapshot_index=2, last_snapshot_term=3, get_last_entry_index=2, get_last_entry_term=2, and then rejected the leader's AppendEntries with PrevLogEntry=2/PrevLogTerm=3 (success=false, no_retry_backoff=true, resp_last_log=2). The otherwise identical control node, with no earlier entry at index 2, reported last_log_index=1, get_last_entry_index=2, get_last_entry_term=3 and accepted the same AppendEntries (success=true, no_retry_backoff=false).\",\n      \"conditions\": \"One process, root package '.', InmemTransport and InmemStore (non-monotonic), server-1 bootstrapped as a Nonvoter so it never campaigns, server-2 acting as the RPC producer; the two sub-cases differ only in whether an earlier-term (term 2) command was first stored at the snapshot index. Applies to the frozen snapshot fd2d6988362c434e9fda87b87c5fb0df.\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"src-installsnap2\", \"src-lastindex2\", \"src-appendentries2\"],\n      \"executions\": { \"72367650c8d0470d8197a7d2c0f97ce1\": [5, 6, 1, 2] }\n    }\n  ],\n  \"gaps\": [\n    {\n      \"investigation_id\": \"c4f67dac947d44fe86d65b317d5d5b4-question-0\",\n      \"question\": \"Reachability: can one compatible multi-node history legally produce the precondition (a follower holding an earlier-term entry at exactly the index where a later-term leader later commits and snapshots), rather than the harness's single seeded AppendEntries, without the follower's higher term forcing the leader to step down?\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"interpretations\": [\n    {\n      \"investigation_id\": \"c4f67dac947d44fe86d65b317d5d5b4-question-0\",\n      \"experiment_id\": \"c4f67dac947d44fe86d65b317d5d5b4-experiment\",\n      \"source_ids\": [\"src-installsnap2\", \"src-lastindex2\", \"src-appendentries2\"],\n      \"executions\": { \"72367650c8d0470d8197a7d2c0f97ce1\": [5, 6, 1, 2] },\n      \"conclusion\": \"violated\",\n      \"defect_claim\": \"asserted\",\n      \"rationale\": \"The compared predicate was that after a successful InstallSnapshot for (L=2,T=3) the node accepts the leader's next AppendEntries with PrevLogEntry=2/PrevLogTerm=3, i.e. post_snapshot_append.success == true. The receipt contradicts it in the defect case and satisfies it in the control, and the paired state observations give the mechanism, so the predicate is violated rather than unknown. Parsed indices in CheckRun 72367650c8d0470d8197a7d2c0f97ce1: index 5 (state_after_snapshot, stale sub-case) shows get_last_entry_term=2 against last_snapshot_term=3 while last_log_index=2 == last_snapshot_index=2, i.e. getLastEntry resolved the index tie in favour of the stale log term; index 6 (post_snapshot_append, stale) shows success=false with no_retry_backoff=true and resp_last_log=2; index 1 (control state) shows last_log_index=1 < last_snapshot_index=2 with get_last_entry_term=3; index 2 (control append) shows success=true. Both nodes installed the snapshot successfully (indices 0 and 4, success=true), so applicability is established by an observed successful InstallSnapshot rather than by assumption, and the only difference between the two sub-cases is the presence of the earlier-term entry at the snapshot index. Scoped defect claim: in hashicorp/raft fd2d6988362c434e9fda87b87c5fb0df, installSnapshot leaves the log-derived last-entry view in place, so a node that already holds an entry at the snapshot index L from an earlier term continues to advertise that stale term for L and rejects the leader's AppendEntries at PrevLogEntry=L/PrevLogTerm=T. The leader-facing consequence is a stable retry cycle: nextIndex = max(min(nextIndex-1, resp.LastLog+1),1) lands on L, setPreviousLog(L) needs the leader's entry L-1, and once the leader has compacted up to its snapshot index that lookup returns ErrLogNotFound, so replicateTo branches to SEND_SNAP and re-sends the same snapshot, restoring nextIndex=L+1 and the same rejection. That cycle is source-sourced and registered as gap c4f67dac947d44fe86d65b317d5d5b4-gap-0 but is not covered by this receipt, which exercised one follower against a driven producer.\",\n      \"counterevidence\": [\n        \"The behind-follower case is not a defect and was observed as the control: with last_log_index=1 below last_snapshot_index=2 the node reports get_last_entry_term=3 and accepts the boundary AppendEntries (index 2, success=true).\",\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
