) sets lastSnapshot=(L,T) but never setLastLog nor invalidates the log entry at L; getLastEntry (state.go 167-174) prefers the log term whenever lastLogIndex >= lastSnapshotIndex, which is exactly the tie for a same-index earlier-term entry; appendEntries (raft.go 1475-1502) then answers Success=false with NoRetryBackoff=true. Leader-facing consequence, source-sourced and still unexecuted: nextIndex=max(min(nextIndex-1,resp.LastLog+1),1) lands on L; setPreviousLog(L) needs the leader's entry L-1; if the leader has compacted up to its snapshot index that lookup is ErrLogNotFound, so replicateTo branches to SEND_SNAP, re-sends the snapshot, restores nextIndex=L+1, and the same rejection recurs.\\\")\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok')\nEOF\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-12_09-55-08-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update-02.json 2>&1 | head -3\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
